[00:00.67]Lesson 5 | 第5课
[00:02.12]The facts | 确切数字
[00:08.68]What was the consequence of the editor's insistence on facts and statistics? | 编辑坚持要事实和数据，结果如何？
[00:16.65]Editors of newspapers and magazines often go to extremes to provide their readers with unimportant facts and statistics. | 报刊杂志的编辑常常走极端，向读者提供一些无关紧要的事实和数据。
[00:25.01]Last year a journalist had been instructed by a well-known magazine to write an article on the president's palace in a new African republic. | 去年，一位记者受一家知名杂志之托，写一篇关于某个新成立的非洲共和国总统府的文章。
[00:35.09]When the article arrived, the editor read the first sentence and then refused to publish it. | 稿子寄到后，编辑看了第一句话便拒绝发表。
[00:42.43]The article began:'Hundreds of steps lead to the high wall which surrounds the president's palace.' | 文章开头是：“几百级台阶通向环绕总统府的高墙。”
[00:50.24]The editor at once sent the journalist a fax instructing him to find out the exact number of steps and the height of the wall. | 编辑立即给记者发了一份传真，要他弄清楚台阶的确切数字和围墙的高度。
[01:01.28]The journalist immediately set out to obtain these important facts, but he took a long time to send them. | 记者随即出发去搜集这些重要事实，但过了很久才把它们发回来。
[01:08.66]Meanwhile, the editor was getting impatient, for the magazine would soon go to press. | 在此期间，编辑等得不耐烦了，因为杂志马上就要付印。
[01:14.24]He sent the journalist two more faxes, but received no reply. | 他又给记者发了两份传真，但仍未见回音。
[01:19.44]He sent yet another fax informing the journalist that if he did not reply soon he would be fired. | 于是他又发了一份传真，通知记者说，若再不速回音便将被解雇。
[01:26.81]When the journalist again failed to reply,  the editor reluctantly published the article as it had originally been written. | 但记者还是没有回复。编辑无奈，只好按原样发表了文章。
[01:35.61]A week later, the editor at last received a fax from the journalist. | 一周之后，编辑终于收到了记者的传真。
[01:40.98]Not only had the poor man been arrested, but he had been sent to prison as well. | 可怜的记者不仅被捕了，而且还被送进了监狱。
[01:47.19]However, he had at last been allowed to send a fax in which he informed the editor that he had been arrested | 不过，他终于获准发回一份传真。他在传真中告诉编辑，
[01:55.99]while counting the 1, 084 steps leading to the 15th foot wall which surrounded the president's palace. | 说他正是在数通向总统府围墙的1084级台阶、丈量那道15英尺高的围墙时被抓的。
